 "brief": "Strongly coupled quantum discrete Liouville theory I: algebraic approach and duality — The quantum discrete Liouville model in the strongly cou- pled regime, 1 < c < 25, is formulated as a well",
 "extended": "**Strongly coupled quantum discrete Liouville theory I: algebraic approach and duality**\n\n*THEORY. I: ALGEBRAIC APPROACH AND DUALITY*\n\n20 pp, 32 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The quantum discrete Liouville model in the strongly cou- pled regime, 1 < c < 25, is formulated as a well deﬁned quantum me- chanical problem with unitary evolution operator. The theory is self- dual: there are two exponential ﬁelds related by Hermitean conjugation, satisfying two discrete quantum Liouville equations, and living in mu- tually commuting subalgebras of the quantum algebra of observables.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; 1 Recollecting the facts; 1.1 Liouville formula and M\"obius-invariance; 1.2 Magri bracket; 1.3 Volterra model; 1.4 Bi-hamiltonity; 1.5 Quantization; 1.6 Proof; 1.7 It has to do with braids; 1.8 Lattice Virasoro algebra; 2 Difference-difference Liouville equation; 2.1 Liouville formula; 2.2 Discrete Liouville equation; 2.3 Poisson bracket; 3 Formal quantization; 3.1 Algebra of observables; 3.2 Quantum lattice Liouville equation",
